## 6. Not verifiable in this environment

A live session against a real `netrewindd`, through the actual compiled
Tauri window: this sandbox can drive browser tabs (used throughout this
work for visual verification) but has no way to launch or interact with a
native OS window, which is what a real Tauri app is - `npm run dev`
serves the same web content a plain browser tab can load, but that tab
never gets Tauri's `__TAURI_INTERNALS__` bridge injected, only the actual
native webview does. What's verified instead: Rust-side logic in
isolation (`cargo test`), and the TypeScript side against a fake `invoke`
matching the real command's exact shape (request/response fields,
cancellation sentinel) byte for byte. The real end-to-end pass - a live
recorder, the compiled installer, real named-pipe/socket traffic - is
Phase 7's job, which already plans exactly this.
